# Every file requires review from the project lead by default.
# See MAINTAINERS.md for the role definitions.
*                       @onyks-os

# Security-critical paths — always require an explicit lead sign-off.
/.github/workflows/     @onyks-os
/SECURITY.md            @onyks-os
/docs/security-assessment.md @onyks-os

# Source paths carrying security-critical logic.
#
# src/rules/     Every byte it parses comes from outside the program, and its
#                output becomes rule syntax. Injection and panics both live here.
# src/dbus/      The trust boundary with the daemon: proxies, the request path,
#                rule-identity handling, and denial attribution.
# Cargo.toml     Adding a dependency, changing a feature set, or relaxing a lint
#                is a change to the attack surface.
/src/rules/             @onyks-os
/src/dbus/              @onyks-os
/Cargo.toml             @onyks-os
/Cargo.lock             @onyks-os
/clippy.toml            @onyks-os
/packaging/             @onyks-os
